Replace the simulated `stage` with your driver, then make the declarations honest. Things you will want next, each a few
lines added to `server.py`:

```python
# measured evidence: use evidence="measured" once a real sensor backs the property
@dev.property(unit="um", evidence="measured", max_rate_hz=10)

# a cancellable action: honour ctx.cancelled and say so
@dev.action(effect="reversible", idempotency="absolute", max_duration_ms=5000, cancel="supported")
async def move_to(ctx, target: Range(0, 200, unit="um")):
    if await ctx.wait_cancelled(0.2):                  # a real driver checks as it moves
        raise Canceled(effect="unverified", detail="stopped early")      # from bhms import Canceled

# a commissioned stop procedure (what `bhms stop` runs)
@dev.on_stop(evidence="reported", max_duration_ms=500)
async def halt(ctx): ...                               # halt motion now

# exclusive access: requires a lease on the resource
@dev.action(effect="irreversible", idempotency="relative", requires_lease=True, max_duration_ms=5000)

# verify an effect by measurement
verified = await ctx.verify("position", lambda v: abs(v - target) < 0.05)
```
